    <item>
      <title>The Fall of Kumbhakarna, the Sleepy Giant</title>
      <description>Today&apos;s story will change how you see everything... In a distant kingdom far, far away, there lived a giant named Kumbhakarna, half-brother of the mighty Ravana. Kumbhakarna&apos;s days were spent sleeping, and his nights spent devouring food with an insatiable appetite. He slept through the dawn, through the day, and into the evening, only to wake up famished, ready to gorge again. Ravana, though mighty, feared his brother - feared his unrelenting hunger, his boundless strength, and his unparalleled ferocity in battle. But when Kumbhakarna slept, Ravana&apos;s kingdom was safe. He could conquer, pillage, and plunder without interruption. And so the king used this knowledge to his advantage, feeding his brother a never-ending supply of food, ensuring he stayed perpetually drowsy. But when Ravana&apos;s plans were threatened by the valiant Rama and his army, he realized his brother&apos;s greatest strength lay in his sleep. He ordered his most skilled chefs to cook the most delicious feast, one that would keep Kumbhakarna asleep forever. And so, Ravana&apos;s kingdom fell, his brother&apos;s insatiable appetite sated, but his kingdom conquered by the mighty Rama. This is Sloth — the refusal to act, to seize the moment, or to live life fully. Today, we procrastinate, we delay, we put off until tomorrow what we could do today. Ask yourself, are you sleeping through life?</description>
      <pubDate>Thu, 09 Apr 2026 14:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
